<title>USA: High Plains Wheat - Interior bids steady to firmer.</title>
<headline>High Plains Wheat - Interior bids steady to firmer.</headline>
<dateline>KANSAS CITY, Mo. 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Basis bids for hard red winter wheat were steady to firmer Wednesday at elevators in Kansas and Oklahoma, dealers there said.</p>
<p>Dealers said movement of wheat remained slow as farmers appeared to be more occupied with harvesting fall crops and planting winter wheat than selling their old crop.</p>
<p>&quot;I think they've put selling on the back burner right now,&quot; a Kansas dealer said.</p>
<p>But farmers' efforts at planting and harvesting looked set to be stymied in coming days due to more rain. Local forecasters expected showers to last through the weekend.  </p>
